              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:20px 0 8px;">
                What Is Fox Hunting?
              </h3>
              <p>
                Amateur Radio Direction Finding (ARDF), commonly called
                &ldquo;fox hunting,&rdquo; is a radio sport where
                participants use directional antennas and signal-strength
                techniques to locate a hidden transmitter &mdash; the
                &ldquo;fox.&rdquo; It combines radio skills, outdoor
                navigation, and teamwork. All license classes are
                welcome, and loaner equipment will be available at
                each event.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:20px 0 8px;">
                How to Get Involved
              </h3>
              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:6px;">
                  <strong>Show up and hunt</strong> &mdash; no
                  prior experience needed; mentors will be present
                  at every event.
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:6px;">
                  <strong>Borrow gear</strong> &mdash; handheld
                  transceivers and tape-measure Yagi antennas
                  available to borrow at the event.
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:6px;">
                  <strong>Stay connected</strong> &mdash; you are
                  already subscribed to this list; watch for
                  individual hunt announcements.
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:6px;">
                  <strong>Spread the word</strong> &mdash; invite
                  a friend or fellow club member who might enjoy the
                  activity.
                </li>
              </ul>

